<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Fossalta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1249">1249</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Fossalta was fought on 26 May 1249 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> between Guelph <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a> and its allies and the Ghibelline forces of Modena and the Emperor Frederick II. The Bolognese captured Frederick's son Enzo, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, who remained their prisoner in Bologna until his death in 1272. The defeat weakened the imperial cause in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-fossalta.jpg" alt="Battle of Fossalta" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Villani, Nouva Cronica, L. VIII, 296, 14th century · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nouva_Cronica_Enzo_von_Sardinien.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
